From 8f1922506233814d686f0a78ed0851fbb55ebfe3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Suresh, Prashanth" <prashanth.suresh@intel.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 05:29:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media-driver: Restore 3 fork-local functional fixes discarded
 by overlay

Found via audit of fork-local commits not reachable from upstream/master,
excluding glue files. All three predate this version bump and were
silently dropped by the intel-media-26.2.3 overlay since they touch
real source files, not Android.bp/Tools/MediaDriverTools/Android glue:

1. media_sku_wa_xe.cpp: restore missing DG2 device ID 0x56AF in
   InitDg2MediaSku's tile-config check (commit 4928886ea).

2. mos_utilities_specific.h: fix USER_FEATURE_FILE* path selection.
   The existing "#if ANDROID_VERSION >= 800" is dead code --
   ANDROID_VERSION is never defined anywhere in this Android.mk build
   -- so the build always fell through to the non-Android /etc/...
   paths, meaning a GPU-hang CTS workaround
   (igfx_user_feature_next.txt, see Enable HCP Scalability
   Decode=0 / Disable Media Encode Scalability=1) would never be
   found at its real /vendor/etc/... location. Restored the fork's
   "#ifdef ANDROID" gate pointing at /vendor/etc/igfx_user_feature*.txt
   (commit 701044217).

3. media_libva.cpp: restore DdiMedia_SelectIntelDevice/
   DdiMedia_IsIntelDgpu device-selection logic (replacing a hardcoded
   DEVICE_NAME), the same dGPU/iGPU selection fix family already found
   and restored in libva's va_android.cpp and (pending) vpl-gpu-rt's
   libmfxsw.cpp. Restored from the final combined state at this fork's
   pre-upgrade HEAD (two commits, 463ae5922 + c5c99e3b4, applied
   sequentially upstream) rather than replaying each commit
   individually, since the second fixes an off-by-128 bug in the first.

Tracked-On: NIACP3-1547
Signed-off-by: Suresh, Prashanth <prashanth.suresh@intel.com>
---
